    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nOn DSv4 EP8, prefill and decode send tokens to very different experts: decode concentrates on a few hot experts, while prefill spreads almost evenly. The same MoE shape therefore wants different kernels in each case. aiter can't tell them apart, because its tuned-config lookup uses only the padded token count, and prefill and decode fall into the same size buckets. Whichever resolves a bucket first fixes the kernel for both, and with CUDA graphs that is always decode. As a result, a decode-tuned table cannot be enabled without also forcing those kernels onto prefill.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the sglang side of a per-regime contract with aiter. An aiter that has the regime API reads one tuned table per regime, from `AITER_CONFIG_FMOE_PREFILL` and `AITER_CONFIG_FMOE_DECODE`.\r\n\r\nCorresponding aiter PR : https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/5821\r\n\r\n## Summary of changes\r\n\r\n- **`layers/moe/aiter_moe_regime.py` (new):**\r\n  - Maps each `ForwardMode` to a regime. `DECODE`, `IDLE` and `TARGET_VERIFY` count as decode. `EXTEND`, `MIXED` and draft-extend count as prefill.\r\n  - Adds `pin_decode_moe_regime()` for use during graph capture.\r\n  - Both do nothing on non-HIP builds or on an aiter without the regime API, so the behaviour there is unchanged.\r\n- **`ModelRunner.forward`:** sets the regime on every forward pass. This is a single delegating call, because `model_runner.py` is frozen.\r\n- **`DecodeCudaGraphRunner.capture`:** pins the decode regime during capture. A replayed graph never re-enters `forward()`, so the kernel chosen at capture time is the one decode keeps using.\r\n\r\n## Results\r\n\r\nSetup: DeepSeek-V4-Pro FP4 on 8Ã MI355X, ISL/OSL 8k/1k, concurrency 128, DP8/EP8 with MoRI a2a, DSpark MTP.\r\n\r\n**Performance**\r\n\r\n| Metric | Baseline | This PR | Delta |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Total token throughput (tok/s) | 26,468.15 | 27,317.32 | +3.21% |\r\n| Output throughput (tok/s) | 2,940.91 | 3,035.26 | +3.21% |\r\n| TPOT mean (ms) | 39.63 | 38.39 | -3.14% |\r\n| TPOT median (ms) | 40.91 | 39.47 | -3.53% |\r\n| TPOT p99 (ms) | 43.23 | 42.25 | -2.28% |\r\n\r\n**Accuracy (gsm8k, 200 questions, 5-shot)**\r\n\r\n| Metric | Baseline | This PR |\r\n|---|---:|---:|\r\n| Accuracy | 0.960 | 0.965 |\r\n| Invalid | 0.000 | 0.000 |\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35994472519](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35994472519)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35994472515](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35994472515)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35994472846](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35994472846)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
